 "explain": "The base text is a collision because the tool slot is unspecified for both verbs, so both compile to one term and their effect laws would fire together. Naming the tools makes the terms distinct and the effects separate. The compiler detects a collision by comparing source verbs (Stage-1 roots) that share one compiled term and have different effect sets; A2.6 says to report it, not to pick one.",
 "notes": "Astra review 5.2: a second availability rule for the same term is not by itself a collision (c10); differing effects are. The Stage-1 projection supplies the roots (boil, fry) and roles the collision check compares; a fixture label would not."
